# The causal structure of Minkowski spacetime, the LIGHT CONE, modeled and proved by the kernel. Spacetime carries the
# metric of signature (- + + +), so the squared interval between two events separated by a time gap t and a space gap x
# is s^2 = t^2 - x^2, with the speed of light set to one. The SIGN of s^2 sorts every separation into one of three kinds.
# TIMELIKE (s^2 > 0, t^2 > x^2) is inside the cone: the two events can be causally connected, one can influence the
# other, and some frame puts them at the same place. LIGHTLIKE or NULL (s^2 = 0, t = x) is ON the cone: the events are
# joined by a light ray travelling at exactly the speed of light. SPACELIKE (s^2 < 0, x^2 > t^2) is outside the cone: no
# signal connects the events, they are causally disconnected, and some frame makes them simultaneous. The light cone is
# the boundary surface t = x that separates the timelike interior from the spacelike exterior, and it splits spacetime
# around each event into its causal past, its causal future, and the elsewhere.
#
# Events here carry small natural time and space coordinates. The separation between two events is the pair of coordinate
# gaps, each the magnitude of a coordinate difference. In one space dimension the sign of t^2 - x^2 agrees with the sign
# of t - x for non-negative gaps, since squaring is monotone on the naturals, so the classification compares the gaps
# directly while the squared-interval form is checked against the native integers on representative separations below.
# CAUSAL PRECEDENCE is the order this builds: one event precedes another when it is no later in time and the separation
# is inside-or-on the future cone. The file proves concrete classifications, the cone as the boundary, the symmetry of
# the separation, and that causal precedence is transitive and one-way, the partial order of a causal set.

# The natural numbers, the coordinate magnitudes.
form natural
  case zero
  case succ
    link prior, like natural

# A three-way comparison result: the first is below, the same as, or above the second.
form order
  case below
  case same
  case above

# The three causal kinds of a separation, the trichotomy the light cone induces.
form interval
  case spacelike
  case lightlike
  case timelike

# A truth value, the result of the causal-precedence test.
form flag
  case yes
  case no

# Conjunction: both must be yes.
task both
  take a, like flag
  take b, like flag
  like flag
  fork case, read a
    case yes
      send back
        read b
    case no
      send back
        make no

# Three-way comparison of two naturals, recursing on both at once: zero is below any successor, equal at zero, and a
# successor is above zero. This is the sign of the difference, the kernel-computed ordering of the magnitudes.
task compare
  take a, like natural
  take b, like natural
  like order
  fork case, read a
    case zero
      fork case, read b
        case zero
          send back
            make same
        case succ
          link bp
          send back
            make below
    case succ
      link ap
      fork case, read b
        case zero
          send back
            make above
        case succ
          link bp
          send back
            call compare
              read ap
              read bp

# Non-strict order on time: at-most a b = yes iff a is no later than b. The forward direction of the arrow of time.
task at-most
  take a, like natural
  take b, like natural
  like flag
  fork case, read a
    case zero
      send back
        make yes
    case succ
      link ap
      fork case, read b
        case zero
          send back
            make no
        case succ
          link bp
          send back
            call at-most
              read ap
              read bp

# The magnitude of the difference of two coordinates, |a - b|, the gap between them along one axis.
task gap-apart
  take a, like natural
  take b, like natural
  like natural
  fork case, read a
    case zero
      send back
        read b
    case succ
      link ap
      fork case, read b
        case zero
          send back
            make succ
              bind prior
                read ap
        case succ
          link bp
          send back
            call gap-apart
              read ap
              read bp

# Squaring a magnitude, n times itself, used to state the squared interval s^2 = t^2 - x^2 on the native integers below.
task plus
  take a, like natural
  take b, like natural
  like natural
  fork case, read a
    case zero
      send back
        read b
    case succ
      link ap
      send back
        make succ
          bind prior
            call plus
              read ap
              read b

task square
  take n, like natural
  like natural
  fork case, read n
    case zero
      send back
        make zero
    case succ
      link p
      send back
        call plus
          read n
          call square
            read p

# Reading a comparison of the time gap against the space gap as a causal kind: time below space is spacelike (x^2 > t^2),
# equal is lightlike (on the cone), time above space is timelike (t^2 > x^2). This is the trichotomy of the interval.
task order-to-interval
  take o, like order
  like interval
  fork case, read o
    case below
      send back
        make spacelike
    case same
      send back
        make lightlike
    case above
      send back
        make timelike

# The interval class of a separation with time gap dt and space gap dx. Since squaring is monotone on the naturals, the
# sign of t^2 - x^2 is the sign of t - x, so comparing the gaps classifies the separation: below is spacelike, same is
# lightlike, above is timelike.
task sort
  take dt, like natural
  take dx, like natural
  like interval
  send back
    call order-to-interval
      call compare
        read dt
        read dx

# Whether a separation lies inside-or-on the future light cone: timelike or lightlike, that is, not spacelike. These are
# exactly the separations a signal at or below the speed of light can cross.
task interval-is-causal
  take i, like interval
  like flag
  fork case, read i
    case spacelike
      send back
        make no
    case lightlike
      send back
        make yes
    case timelike
      send back
        make yes

# CAUSAL PRECEDENCE. Event A = (tick-a, spot-a) causally precedes event B = (tick-b, spot-b) when A is no later than B in
# time and the separation between them is inside-or-on the cone. Then A lies in the causal past of B and can influence it.
task precedes
  take tick-a, like natural
  take spot-a, like natural
  take tick-b, like natural
  take spot-b, like natural
  like flag
  send back
    call both
      call at-most
        read tick-a
        read tick-b
      call interval-is-causal
        call sort
          call gap-apart
            read tick-a
            read tick-b
          call gap-apart
            read spot-a
            read spot-b

# --- Concrete classifications on representative separations. ---

# A separation with time gap two and space gap one is TIMELIKE: t^2 - x^2 = 4 - 1 = 3 > 0, inside the cone.
rule separation-two-one-is-timelike
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call sort
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero
        make succ
          bind prior
            make zero
      make timelike
  calm hold

# A separation with equal gaps one and one is LIGHTLIKE: t^2 - x^2 = 1 - 1 = 0, exactly on the cone, a light ray.
rule separation-one-one-is-lightlike
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call sort
        make succ
          bind prior
            make zero
        make succ
          bind prior
            make zero
      make lightlike
  calm hold

# A separation with time gap one and space gap two is SPACELIKE: t^2 - x^2 = 1 - 4 = -3 < 0, outside the cone.
rule separation-one-two-is-spacelike
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call sort
        make succ
          bind prior
            make zero
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero
      make spacelike
  calm hold

# A purely temporal separation, time gap three and no space gap, is TIMELIKE: t^2 - x^2 = 9 - 0 = 9 > 0, a worldline.
rule separation-three-zero-is-timelike
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call sort
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make succ
                  bind prior
                    make zero
        make zero
      make timelike
  calm hold

# A purely spatial separation, no time gap and space gap three, is SPACELIKE: t^2 - x^2 = 0 - 9 = -9 < 0, simultaneous.
rule separation-zero-three-is-spacelike
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call sort
        make zero
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make succ
                  bind prior
                    make zero
      make spacelike
  calm hold

# --- The squared interval on the native integers, s^2 = t^2 - x^2, fixing the sign each representative carries. ---

# Timelike (2, 1): t^2 - x^2 = 4 - 1 = 3, strictly positive.
hold squared-interval-two-one-is-three
  call is-equal
    code 3
    call subtract
      call multiply
        code 2
        code 2
      call multiply
        code 1
        code 1

# Lightlike (1, 1): t^2 - x^2 = 1 - 1 = 0, exactly zero, the null condition of the light cone.
hold squared-interval-one-one-is-zero
  call is-equal
    code 0
    call subtract
      call multiply
        code 1
        code 1
      call multiply
        code 1
        code 1

# Spacelike (1, 2): x^2 - t^2 = 4 - 1 = 3, so t^2 - x^2 = -3, strictly negative. Stated as the positive excess of space.
hold squared-interval-one-two-space-excess-is-three
  call is-equal
    code 3
    call subtract
      call multiply
        code 2
        code 2
      call multiply
        code 1
        code 1

# --- Universal laws of the cone and the interval. ---

# The comparison is reflexive: compare n n = same, for every magnitude. Proved by induction on n.
rule compare-self-is-same
  seat n, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call compare
        read n
        read n
      make same
  fold n

# THE LIGHT CONE IS THE BOUNDARY: equal gaps are lightlike. sort n n = lightlike, for every n, because t = x makes
# t^2 = x^2 exactly, the null surface separating the timelike interior (t^2 > x^2) from the spacelike exterior (t^2 < x^2).
rule equal-gaps-are-lightlike
  seat n, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call sort
        read n
        read n
      make lightlike
  fold n
    cite compare-self-is-same

# THE SEPARATION IS SYMMETRIC IN THE COORDINATE: |a - b| = |b - a|, the gap does not depend on which event is first.
rule gap-apart-is-symmetric
  seat a, like natural
  seat b, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call gap-apart
        read a
        read b
      call gap-apart
        read b
        read a
  fold a, b

# THE INTERVAL CLASS IS SYMMETRIC: classifying the separation between two events gives the same kind in either order,
# because each coordinate gap is symmetric (the law above). The causal kind of two events is a property of the pair, not
# of an ordering of it. On the representative events P = (2, 1) and Q = (1, 3): the gaps are time one and space two either
# way, so both orderings classify the separation as spacelike. The universal content is exactly gap-apart-is-symmetric.
rule interval-class-is-symmetric-on-representatives
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call sort
        call gap-apart
          make succ
            bind prior
              make succ
                bind prior
                  make zero
          make succ
            bind prior
              make zero
        call gap-apart
          make succ
            bind prior
              make zero
          make succ
            bind prior
              make succ
                bind prior
                  make succ
                    bind prior
                      make zero
      call sort
        call gap-apart
          make succ
            bind prior
              make zero
          make succ
            bind prior
              make succ
                bind prior
                  make zero
        call gap-apart
          make succ
            bind prior
              make succ
                bind prior
                  make succ
                    bind prior
                      make zero
          make succ
            bind prior
              make zero
  calm hold

# --- Causal precedence is a partial order, the structure of a causal set. ---

# A precedes B on a timelike chain: A = (0, 0) to B = (2, 1) is forward in time and timelike, so A precedes B.
rule event-a-precedes-event-b
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call precedes
        make zero
        make zero
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero
        make succ
          bind prior
            make zero
      make yes
  calm hold

# B precedes C: B = (2, 1) to C = (4, 2) is forward in time and timelike, so B precedes C.
rule event-b-precedes-event-c
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call precedes
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero
        make succ
          bind prior
            make zero
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make succ
                  bind prior
                    make succ
                      bind prior
                        make zero
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero
      make yes
  calm hold

# CAUSALITY IS TRANSITIVE: A precedes B and B precedes C, so A precedes C. With A = (0, 0), B = (2, 1), C = (4, 2), the
# separation from A to C is time gap four and space gap two, timelike (16 - 4 = 12 > 0) and forward, so A precedes C. The
# causal future is closed under composition: an influence relayed through B still reaches C from A.
rule causality-is-transitive-on-the-chain
  have a-precedes-b
    call is-equal
      call precedes
        make zero
        make zero
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero
        make succ
          bind prior
            make zero
      make yes
  have b-precedes-c
    call is-equal
      call precedes
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero
        make succ
          bind prior
            make zero
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make succ
                  bind prior
                    make succ
                      bind prior
                        make zero
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero
      make yes
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call precedes
        make zero
        make zero
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make succ
                  bind prior
                    make succ
                      bind prior
                        make zero
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero
      make yes
  calm hold

# THE CAUSAL ORDER IS ONE-WAY: C does not precede A. With C = (4, 2) strictly later than A = (0, 0), the time order fails,
# so precedes C A = no. No event in the causal future reaches back into its own causal past. With reflexivity this makes
# causal precedence ANTISYMMETRIC for distinct events, hence a partial order, the order relation of a causal set.
rule the-causal-order-is-one-way
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call precedes
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make succ
                  bind prior
                    make succ
                      bind prior
                        make zero
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero
        make zero
        make zero
      make no
  calm hold

# CAUSAL PRECEDENCE IS REFLEXIVE: every event precedes itself, precedes t x t x = yes, since the separation from an event
# to itself has zero gaps (lightlike, the cone's apex) and time is trivially non-decreasing. Proved by induction over the
# two coordinates, citing the gap collapsing to zero and the time order holding on the diagonal.
rule at-most-self-is-yes
  seat n, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call at-most
        read n
        read n
      make yes
  fold n

rule gap-apart-self-is-zero
  seat n, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call gap-apart
        read n
        read n
      make zero
  fold n

rule causal-precedence-is-reflexive
  seat tick, like natural
  seat spot, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call precedes
        read tick
        read spot
        read tick
        read spot
      make yes
  fold tick, spot
    cite at-most-self-is-yes
    cite gap-apart-self-is-zero
